To find the characteristic polynomial of a matrix $ A $, we compute the determinant of $ A - \lambda I $, where $ I $ is the identity matrix and $ \lambda $ is a scalar. The matrix given is:

$$
A = \begin{pmatrix}
14 & \frac{22}{3} & 2 \\
\frac{20}{3} & -\frac{38}{3} & \frac{10}{3} \\
-\frac{22}{3} & \frac{40}{3} & \frac{10}{3}
\end{pmatrix}
$$

Subtracting $ \lambda $ from the diagonal entries, we get:

$$
A - \lambda I = \begin{pmatrix}
14 - \lambda & \frac{22}{3} & 2 \\
\frac{20}{3} & -\frac{38}{3} - \lambda & \frac{10}{3} \\
-\frac{22}{3} & \frac{40}{3} & \frac{10}{3} - \lambda
\end{pmatrix}
$$

The determinant is calculated using cofactor expansion along the first row. After computing each 2x2 determinant and simplifying, the characteristic polynomial is found to be:

$$
\lambda^3 - 270 \lambda^2 + \frac{678}{3} \lambda - \frac{2872}{9}
$$
